  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The 1st ed. (Faenza : 1918) was the 1st book of asemantic writings. Martini's 40 woodcuts consist of rows of black rectangles arrayed between pairs of horizontal lines, like words of poetry or notes of music (cf. Artist and book in twentieth century Italy).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cover title.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Questo volumetto a cura di Silvano e Vanni Scheiwiller è l'editione in facsimile di Contemplazioni, prima e seconda edizione, ed è stato impresso a Milano dalla Tipografia U. Allegretti di Campi in mille copie numerate da 1 a 1000"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The words "Edizione in facsimile dei legni originali 1918" and the imprint appear on a slip of green paper mounted on p. [3] of cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Allegato a Contemplazioni, 1967: Le 'Contemplazioni 1936' nel ricordo di Carlo Scarpa"--Leaves [1]-[2].</subfield>
